This is my first ascension on NAO; as I usually do, I selected my character 
randomly.
My general strategy was to pick up daggers and use those as my primary weapons; 
I didn't want to use all of my crossbow ammo and be helpless. This worked well, 
and I eventually swapped them for elven daggers. I kept my crossbow and bolts, 
with crossbow experience at skilled, for tougher targets. I picked up all arrows 
I found, though, and by the time I finished the quest, I had several hundred. 
Eventually, I got tired of collecting them, so I canceled them and enchanted 
them up. I ended up with 915 blessed poisoned rustproof +7 arrows. Overkill, 
yes, but it gave me a nice sense of power. I stashed 450 or so, put 350 in my 
bag of holding, and kept another 100 in my main inventory. These were awesome; I 
maxed my luck so I only rarely lost them, and two or three volleys were usually 
enough to kill most nasties, such as liches and mind flayers. Near the end of 
the game, I took out arrows in sets of 100 and tried to enchant them further. I 
got lucky and ended up with 200 +8 arrows after just three tries. The bottom 
line is that arrows deal awesome damage.
I also chose jumping boots over speed boots; these let me get away from anything 
that couldn't teleport, and as an archer, the space was wonderful. If something 
got too close, I just jumped away and continued shooting.
I chose an oilskin cloak, as I would be wearing a shield for reflection, and 
already had GDSM. I wore a amulet of magical breathing, which was very nice, and 
as I only needed a full healing potion once, in the sanctum, I didn't miss 
life-saving.
For melee, I went for the Vorpal Blade; in melee, I didn't need to do much 
damage, as I would only rarely be fighting tough monsters that way. I didn't 
even bother enchanting it (and then only to +3) until right before the ascension 
run. The beheading attack was what proved very useful, both against the Wizard, 
and against teleporting liches.
I didn't genocide anything just because I didn't feel like it.
On the Astral plane, wore conflict and free action. I killed the hostile angels 
easily, then went to the nearest altar. I waited in front of the door until 
Death opened it, then I filled him with arrows. I ran through, killed some 
Angels who blocked my path, then ran to the next door. There was only one Angel 
in my way, so I teleported him and jumped strait into the temple. I shut and 
locked the door, and was please to find that it was the right altar.


